  The reel_script says the headmistress Komathi went on leave for 2 days due to illness, but the article only says she took leave; the 'உடல்நலக் குறைவால்' reason and '2 நாட்கள்' duration are in the article, so this is fine, but the caption and reel_script both say 'உதவி ஆசிரியர் செந்தில்குமார்' took leave 'கடந்த ஜூலை மாதம் முதல்' — the article says he has taken frequent leave since July, which matches.
  The reel_script states that the substitute teacher 'நியமிக்கப்பட்டிருந்தார்' (was appointed) and that 'ஆசிரியர்கள் இருவரும் மாற்றுப்பணி ஆசிரியரும் வரவில்லை' — the article says the substitute did not come, which matches.
  The caption says '21 மாணவர்களும் பள்ளி வளாகத்திலும் சாலையிலும் சுற்றினர்' and the reel says the same; the article supports this.
  The caption states the headmistress is 'தலைமை ஆசிரியர் கோமதி' and the slide says the same; article matches.
  The caption's 'வகுப்பறை பூட்டி கிடந்தது' is in the article, but the caption and reel_script conflate 'nothing came' with the classroom being locked as a cause from the absence; the article says the classroom was locked because the teachers did not come, which matches.
  The reel_script phrase 'வேறு பள்ளியிலிருந்து மாற்றுப்பணி ஆசிரியர் நியமிக்கப்பட்டிருந்தார்' is placed in a sentence about Senthilkumar's leave, mixing two facts (the reason for the substitute appointment is his frequent leave, which the article does state), so this is acceptable.
  The reel_script omits that the school was opened only after an outside teacher was summoned, but it does include this; no key omission identified regarding arrest or action since no arrest occurred and the article's action is the show-cause notice, which is included.
